# Dropbox Sync Exclusions for ANBU Landing Page
# NOTE: Dropbox doesn't officially support .dropboxignore files
# You must manually exclude these folders using Selective Sync in Dropbox settings
# 
# To exclude these folders:
# 1. Right-click Dropbox icon in system tray
# 2. Click Preferences/Settings
# 3. Go to "Sync" tab
# 4. Click "Selective Sync" or "Choose folders to sync"
# 5. Uncheck these folders within your ANBU_Landing_Page project:

# Platform-specific dependencies (MUST EXCLUDE)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Build outputs (SHOULD EXCLUDE)
.next/
**/.next/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
out/
**/out/

# Cache directories (SHOULD EXCLUDE)
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
.cache/
**/.cache/
.parcel-cache/
**/.parcel-cache/

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp

# Lock files (BE CAREFUL - these should sync but can cause conflicts)
# If you have issues, exclude these and manage manually:
# pnpm-lock.yaml
# package-lock.json
# yarn.lock

# Docker volumes (MUST EXCLUDE)
docker/volumes/
.docker/

# IDE specific
.idea/
.vscode-server/

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# ================
# 1. After excluding node_modules, you MUST run 'pnpm install' on each machine
# 2. The pnpm-lock.yaml file SHOULD sync to maintain consistency
# 3. If you get conflicts on pnpm-lock.yaml, accept the most recent version
# 4. Always use Docker for development to avoid platform issues
# 5. Run 'pnpm docker:setup' when switching machines